<title>INDIA: Indian coalminers defer three-day strike.</title>
<headline>Indian coalminers defer three-day strike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A proposed strike by nearly 750,000 coalminers in India has been deferred after an assurance from Prime Minister Inder Kumar Gujral that further talks would be held to consider their demands, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said on Friday.</p>
<p>PTI quoted a statement from labour unions as saying that the strike was deferred as Gujral had assured the unions that further discussions would start with their members in a week.</p>
<p>On Thursday the coalminers, who are protesting against the government's move to privatise the coal sector, said that they would go on a three-day strike from July 28 as talks with the government had failed.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
